var e=JSON.parse('"---\\ntitle: \\"How to Brainstorm Carousel Topics with AI\\"\\nslug: \\"how-to-brainstorm-carousel-topics-with-ai\\"\\nlanguage: \\"en\\"\\ndescription: \\"Learn how to brainstorm endless carousel topics using AI. Stop staring at a blank page and generate high-converting ideas for LinkedIn and Instagram.\\"\\nprimaryKeyword: \\"brainstorm carousel topics with ai\\"\\nsecondaryKeywords:\\n  - \\"carousel post ideas\\"\\n  - \\"linkedin topics\\"\\n  - \\"instagram carousel ideas\\"\\n  - \\"content matrix\\"\\n  - \\"ai content generation\\"\\nsearchIntent: \\"user wants a system or prompts to generate relevant and engaging topics for their social media carousels using AI tools\\"\\ncluster: \\"AI Carousel Ideas\\"\\narticleType: \\"how_to\\"\\ncategory: \\"Content Strategy\\"\\npriority: \\"P1\\"\\npublished: true\\nnoindex: false\\npreview: false\\napprovedForPublish: true\\ncanonical: \\"https://gotoflow.io/blog/how-to-brainstorm-carousel-topics-with-ai\\"\\ncreatedAt: \\"2026-06-17\\"\\nupdatedAt: \\"2026-10-10\\"\\nlastReviewed: \\"2026-06-18\\"\\nmockupStatus: \\"not_available\\"\\nmockupReason: \\"No exact asset provided in brief\\"\\nkeywordRecord: \\"how to brainstorm carousel topics with AI\\"\\ntopicScoreId: \\"TS-23-12\\"\\nfinalPriorityScore: 84\\npriorityTier: \\"P1\\"\\nproductCapabilityIds: [\\"textToCarousel\\"]\\nintentId: \\"en:how-to-brainstorm-carousel-topics-with-ai\\"\\nclusterId: \\"en:ai-carousel-generator\\"\\narticleRole: \\"supporting\\"\\nhubSlug: \\"text-to-carousel-ai\\"\\nrelatedProductRoute: \\"/ai-carousel-maker\\"\\nproductFit: \\"YES\\"\\nproductFitExplanation: \\"GoToFlow helps creators turn brainstormed topics into fully structured ready-to-publish carousels.\\"\\nrequiredVisualBlock: \\"none\\"\\nfaqFormat: \\"structured\\"\\nqualityGateStatus: \\"passed\\"\\nquickAnswerTitle: \\"Quick Answer\\"\\nquickAnswer:\\n  - \\"The blank page is your enemy. Use AI to generate a content matrix intersecting your niche with proven formats.\\"\\n  - \\"Don\'t just ask AI for \'post ideas\'. Give it context about your audience, their pain points, and your product.\\"\\n  - \\"Break broad topics (e.g., \'Digital Marketing\') into micro-topics (e.g., \'3 SEO mistakes killing your blog traffic\').\\"\\n  - \\"Use specific prompts to generate hooks, not just boring titles.\\"\\n  - \\"Once you have a topic and source material, use GoToFlow to generate slide structure, copy, and design; review the result before export.\\"\\nfaq:\\n  - question: \\"Why do I run out of ideas for carousels?\\"\\n    answer: \\"You are likely trying to create broad, textbook-style posts. The best carousels focus on hyper-specific micro-problems. Instead of \'How to invest,\' write \'How I invest $100 a month in ETFs\'.\\"\\n  - question: \\"How is AI better at brainstorming than me?\\"\\n    answer: \\"AI can propose angles from the brief you provide. Compare the suggestions with your audience\'s actual questions and available sources; this guide does not verify a processing time or a count of frameworks consulted.\\"\\n  - question: \\"What is a content matrix?\\"\\n    answer: \\"A content matrix is a framework where you list your core topics on one axis (e.g., Copywriting, SEO) and formats on the other (e.g., Mistakes, How-to, Case Study). Intersecting them gives you endless ideas.\\"\\n  - question: \\"Should I let AI write the whole post after picking a topic?\\"\\n    answer: \\"No. Let AI generate the structure and slide breakdown, but inject your own expertise, stories, and tone of voice into the content.\\"\\n  - question: \\"How many topics should I brainstorm at once?\\"\\n    answer: \\"Set a planning session, ask for candidate topics, and retain only those with a clear reader question and a usable source. The time, accepted topic count, and calendar coverage depend on your brief and review; no fixed yield is established here.\\"\\nexplore:\\n  tools:\\n    - title: \\"AI Carousel Maker\\"\\n      href: \\"/ai-carousel-maker\\"\\n      description: \\"Turn topics and sources into carousels, then review and export.\\"\\n  guides:\\n    - title: \\"30 Social Media Ideas\\"\\n      href: \\"/blog/social-media-post-ideas-for-business\\"\\n      description: \\"Proven post ideas for small businesses.\\"\\n    - title: \\"Viral LinkedIn Hooks\\"\\n      href: \\"/blog/viral-linkedin-post-examples\\"\\n      description: \\"Breakdown of 10 viral hooks.\\"\\nfinalCta:\\n  title: \\"Have a great topic but no time to design?\\"\\n  text: \\"Stop wrestling with blank slides. Turn your rough topic into a structured carousel, then review and export.\\"\\n  buttonText: \\"Create a Carousel with AI\\"\\n  microcopy: \\"Free — No credit card required\\"\\n  secondaryText: \\"AI Content Marketing Strategy →\\"\\n  secondaryHref: \\"/blog/ai-content-marketing-strategy\\"\\n---\\n\\n# How to Brainstorm Carousel Topics with AI\\n\\nStaring at a blank screen is the most expensive part of content creation. You know your industry inside out, yet when it’s time to write a LinkedIn or Instagram carousel, your mind goes completely blank.\\n\\nYou end up writing a generic post, nobody saves it, and the cycle repeats. \\n\\nUsing AI for brainstorming changes this dynamic. It shifts you from being an exhausted writer trying to invent ideas from scratch to an editor curating the best angles. \\n\\n## The Core Strategy: The Content Matrix\\n\\nTo never run out of ideas, you need a system. The Content Matrix is a proven method used by top creators, and AI is highly effective at populating it.\\n\\nThe matrix is simple: you cross **Core Pillars** (what you know) with **Proven Formats** (how people consume content).\\n\\n:::cards\\ntype: takeaways\\n\\n### 1. Core Pillars\\nIdentify 3-4 main topics you talk about. If you are a designer, these might be UI/UX, Typography, Freelancing, and Tools.\\n\\n### 2. Proven Formats\\nIdentify how information is best delivered. The most popular formats are: Step-by-Step, Common Mistakes, Myths, Case Studies, and Tools.\\n\\n### 3. The Intersection\\nCombine them. \\"Typography\\" + \\"Mistakes\\" = *5 Typography Mistakes That Make Your UI Look Cheap*. \\n:::\\n\\n> [!tip]\\n> **Don\'t go too broad**\\n> Narrow a broad topic (“How to design a website”) to a question you can answer (“What should a hero section explain before signup?”). Do not invent a conversion percentage to make the hook specific.\\n\\n## Generating Topics with AI Prompts\\n\\nIf you just type \\"give me ideas for carousels\\" into an AI, you will get generic garbage. You must provide context: who you are, who you serve, and what format you want.\\n\\nUse these proven prompt frameworks to generate high-quality topics.\\n\\n:::prompts\\n### The Pain Point Extractor\\n```text\\nI am a [Your Profession]. My target audience is [Describe Audience]. \\nList 10 specific, daily frustrations they face regarding [Your Niche]. \\nFor each frustration, suggest a \\"How-to\\" carousel topic that solves it.\\n```\\n\\n### The Matrix Filler\\n```text\\nMy core topic is [Topic]. Give me 5 carousel ideas based on these formats: \\n1) A controversial opinion or myth, 2) A step-by-step framework, \\n3) A list of common mistakes, 4) A \\"Before and After\\" case study, \\n5) A list of recommended tools.\\n```\\n\\n### The Hook Generator\\n```text\\nI want to write a carousel about [Specific Topic]. \\nGenerate 10 punchy, curiosity-driven hooks for the first slide. \\nThey should be under 10 words and make the reader want to swipe.\\n```\\n:::\\n\\n## From Topic to Structured Carousel\\n\\nHaving a great topic is only the starting point. The next challenge is structuring that idea into a readable, engaging 10-slide presentation.\\nOnce you have selected an angle, use the [text-to-carousel guide](/blog/text-to-carousel-ai) to develop the source message into a slide sequence rather than treating the topic list as finished copy.\\n\\nMany creators drop the ball here. They take a great topic but dump all the information onto three crowded slides. \\n\\n> [!tip]\\n> **Turn ideas into slides effortlessly**\\n> Don\'t waste hours formatting text. Paste your brainstormed topic or rough notes into GoToFlow, and our system will automatically structure it into a slide-by-slide ready-to-publish carousel.\\n> [Try AI Carousel Maker](/ai-carousel-maker)\\n\\n## Common Brainstorming Pitfalls\\n\\nEven with AI, you can generate the wrong type of content. Watch out for these traps:\\n\\n:::cards\\ntype: mistakes\\n\\n### 1. Writing for your peers\\nIf your audience is beginners, don\'t brainstorm complex, jargon-heavy topics that only your competitors will understand.\\n\\n### 2. Lack of actionable advice\\n\\"The History of Marketing\\" is a bad carousel. \\"3 Marketing Tactics You Can Use Today\\" is a highly savable carousel.\\n\\n### 3. Ignoring the CTA\\nEvery topic must align with a business goal. If you brainstorm a topic but can\'t naturally tie it to a Call to Action on the final slide, discard it.\\n:::\\n\\n> [!related]\\n> **Read next**\\n> Once you have your topic, learn how to refine your strategy in our [AI Carousel Content Strategy Guide](/blog/ai-carousel-content-strategy).\\n\\n## Conclusion\\n\\nBrainstorming shouldn\'t be a daily struggle. By utilizing AI to map out your content matrix, you can organise candidate topics for your next planning cycle, then check their sources and usefulness before production.\\n\\nOnce you have your winning topics, stop doing the heavy lifting of design and layout manually. Use smart workflow tools to transform those ideas into publish-ready carousels, allowing you to focus on strategy and engaging with your audience.\\n"');export{e as default};